                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ad05c20d-ee7a-34be-98ca-b0b4389c7ece",
                        "entry_id": "616ce148-0a09-3447-8e8a-42bf91e297d7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "бить, колотить с напором, остервенением"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c37dd3d5-6d19-4cde-8e8d-11543207ecdc",
                                "sense_id": "ad05c20d-ee7a-34be-98ca-b0b4389c7ece",
                                "text": "Потому что, заметив порванную уздечку, он пришел в неописуемую ярость, схватил валявшееся тут же полено и, придерживая своего осла за порванную уздечку, стал изо всех сил колошматить его по спине."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8aab0ff2-ef55-4c66-81e2-7a3f35c396b8",
                                "sense_id": "ad05c20d-ee7a-34be-98ca-b0b4389c7ece",
                                "text": "Так что, слово за слово, ну она и вцепилась в его свитер и давай колошматить…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e81b65a-7a5b-4231-ab71-4f3d3db8e137",
                                "sense_id": "ad05c20d-ee7a-34be-98ca-b0b4389c7ece",
                                "text": "― быстро сквозь зубы спросила у Жени девчонка, не переставая колошматить козу пинками."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "30825f34-125e-47b5-a156-0b1fe1c4176b",
                        "source_entry_id": "616ce148-0a09-3447-8e8a-42bf91e297d7",
                        "source_sense_id": "ad05c20d-ee7a-34be-98ca-b0b4389c7ece",
                        "target_lang_word": "clobber",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "clobber",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f705209e-2118-3a46-9b54-48629d056f81",
                                        "entry_id": "3f5aa686-9f04-3ff7-a89d-82452771e8f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To hit or bash severely; to seriously harm or damage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c9cd6a6-a822-43f9-9826-d1170015a322",
                                                "sense_id": "f705209e-2118-3a46-9b54-48629d056f81",
                                                "text": "So the temptation to clobber was always there, and it was sometimes more difficult not to strike than it would have been to strike, and the consequences be damned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ac074f4-6d6b-42ae-92f8-df0c564a0977",
                                                "sense_id": "f705209e-2118-3a46-9b54-48629d056f81",
                                                "text": "2000 November 30, Kenya National Assembly Official Record (Hansard), page 3034,\nMr. Speaker, Sir, in the East African Standard newspaper we saw a picture of a man being carried away after being clobbered. We also saw women being clobbered by well-built policemen using big clubs. They were clobbering women who had already fallen on the ground."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "910e91fa-401d-42ed-bfe8-b14e81d38cad",
                                                "sense_id": "f705209e-2118-3a46-9b54-48629d056f81",
                                                "text": "Most of the job of the UNIX Oracle DBA is keeping the database running, and it does not come as a surprise when they see how easy it is to clobber a server.\nThe following script cripples the UNIX server by an implosion of incoming jobs. This is known as a denial of service (DOS) attack[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c05e1ed-f157-3e55-8fa9-5c1ededc9171",
                                        "entry_id": "3f5aa686-9f04-3ff7-a89d-82452771e8f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To overwrite (data) or override (an assignment of a value), often unintentionally or unexpectedly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "381d2342-9420-4943-bbe0-b3df5981f7a0",
                                                "sense_id": "7c05e1ed-f157-3e55-8fa9-5c1ededc9171",
                                                "text": "It is therefore clear that the system itself must be truly \"clobber proof\"; that is, no user may be capable of changing anyone else's program or tying up the system in any way that would disrupt normal service to other users."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "265f0c24-d902-4193-9a85-3b688cbe4d64",
                                                "sense_id": "7c05e1ed-f157-3e55-8fa9-5c1ededc9171",
                                                "text": "In the slang of computer programmers, the second re-entry address is likely to \"clobber\" the machine's memory of the original re-entry address."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d992422-6d70-4155-b2ab-fc783f1accc4",
                                                "sense_id": "7c05e1ed-f157-3e55-8fa9-5c1ededc9171",
                                                "text": "Inferences made in accordance with this reason are defeated by finding that the merged plan clobbers one of the causal-links in one of the constituent plans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d331e6b-f022-45ea-8d83-e361b9d65679",
                                                "sense_id": "7c05e1ed-f157-3e55-8fa9-5c1ededc9171",
                                                "text": "The cp command does one thing as it clobbers a file; mv and ln do another."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3e27b7f-cb4d-48c7-8e25-fd9817bca041",
                                                "sense_id": "7c05e1ed-f157-3e55-8fa9-5c1ededc9171",
                                                "text": "These functions collide, and we can see in Figure 7-1 that the debug() function for SexyWidgets clobbers the developer′s debug() function. The last function declared with the same name in the same scope will silently clobber the earlier function definition."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4a4f9bd-7ed9-4f55-91f3-bdb07a6bda29",
                                                "sense_id": "7c05e1ed-f157-3e55-8fa9-5c1ededc9171",
                                                "text": "If you create your own mood instance attribute without being aware of the name clash, you will clobber the mood attribute used by the methods inherited from Dog."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "clobber",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfef3437-06fe-3149-b49a-201415b65608",
                                        "entry_id": "cc1b93f0-e5b4-33b9-a691-b37967ffacab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A thumping or beating."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2978946a-334a-4c51-9717-c93bf0400573",
                                                "sense_id": "cfef3437-06fe-3149-b49a-201415b65608",
                                                "text": "He should have stepped back and given Hemi room to chat and see where the women^([sic]) was going, yet he found himself drawn over to them. His friend would probably give him a clobber later on for his stupidity […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "836d1452-c7c4-388d-bc49-b092587c7bbe",
                                        "entry_id": "cc1b93f0-e5b4-33b9-a691-b37967ffacab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bash on say the head, typically with a tool or object rather than with fists."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "clobber",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03f5fce7-88ee-3f04-af47-23ac5c7e4cb7",
                                        "entry_id": "44315bfc-0a82-3d5e-9e4e-906ce6137c17",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Clothing; clothes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "British",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "270ed2fe-e300-44b9-a3f1-360cc5a08f3c",
                                                "sense_id": "03f5fce7-88ee-3f04-af47-23ac5c7e4cb7",
                                                "text": "W'y, they call a man a robber if 'e stuffs 'is marchin' clobber / With the— / (Chorus) Loo! loo! Lulu! lulu! Loo! loo! Loot! loot! loot!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "869e778b-06db-472a-868d-b72e58dc9c3b",
                                                "sense_id": "03f5fce7-88ee-3f04-af47-23ac5c7e4cb7",
                                                "text": "Now to get rid of this respectable clobber and feel like a man again."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e58a9246-dd89-4cac-a355-cba3e0952d42",
                                                "sense_id": "03f5fce7-88ee-3f04-af47-23ac5c7e4cb7",
                                                "text": "I was thinkin' of the widow while I gets me clobber on— / Like a feller will start thinkin' of the times that's past an' gone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3c6cb85-dd39-4dec-8f30-4e1dd2e30c8b",
                                                "sense_id": "03f5fce7-88ee-3f04-af47-23ac5c7e4cb7",
                                                "text": "I went to one in Woolwich, south-east London, which is one of the first stores to welcome the Pep&Co range, to road test the new uber-cheap clobber for myself."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e2ba764-8d24-3ec1-bd41-b16b9a394e8e",
                                        "entry_id": "44315bfc-0a82-3d5e-9e4e-906ce6137c17",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Equipment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
